---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../components/ui/Section.astro";
import Label from "../components/ui/Label.astro";
import Button from "../components/ui/Button.astro";
import CostCurve from "../components/CostCurve.astro";
const ladder = (await getCollection("ladder")).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const faqs = (await getCollection("faqs")).find((f) => f.data.page === "homepage");
---
<Base
  title="Reardon Systems — Modern Private/Hybrid Cloud for Mid-Market"
  description="Cut cloud bill shock, escape lock-in, and run AI/GPU workloads on infrastructure you control — without losing developer velocity."
>
<!-- HERO -->
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy text-white">
  <div class="grid-lines absolute inset-0 opacity-40"></div>
  <div class="absolute -right-40 -top-40 h-[36rem] w-[36rem] rounded-full bg-electric/20 blur-3xl"></div>
  <div class="relative mx-auto grid max-w-8xl items-center gap-12 px-6 pb-28 pt-24 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium tracking-wide text-white/80">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-signal"></span>
        For mid-market teams spending $500K–$10M+ on cloud
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-electric">
        Not anti-cloud. Anti-default.
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black leading-[1.05] tracking-tight md:text-6xl">
        Show us the bill that hurts.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/80 md:text-xl">
        Mid-market teams with real hyperscaler spend. Reardon Systems turns the
        bill into a workload map, a TCO model, and a pilot that finance and
        engineering can both defend.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <Button href="/contact">Start with an Assessment</Button>
        <Button href="/engagements" variant="ghost">See engagements</Button>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-xs text-white/60">
        <span>✓ Fixed scope</span>
        <span>✓ Infra pass-through stays separate</span>
        <span>✓ Optional savings-share</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-white/60">
          <span>Annual cloud spend</span>
          <span class="font-semibold text-signal">Cloud-only</span>
        </div>
        <CostCurve />
        <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-xs">
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-white/5 p-3">
            <div class="text-white/60">Egress</div>
            <div class="mt-1 font-semibold">Eliminated</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-white/5 p-3">
            <div class="text-white/60">GPU</div>
            <div class="mt-1 font-semibold">Owned</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-white/5 p-3">
            <div class="text-white/60">DX</div>
            <div class="mt-1 font-semibold">Unchanged</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<!-- PROBLEM -->
<Section>
  <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <Label color="signal">The problem</Label>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-4xl">
        The bill is not the problem. The default is.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate lg:col-span-7">
      <p>
        Every dollar of steady-state compute you rent by the hour is a dollar
        you already decided to spend. Every egress charge is a tax on your own
        data. Every GPU provisioned just in case is margin you will never see
        again.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        And someone in the room will ask the same question:
        <em>will developers lose velocity?</em>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 font-medium text-navy">
        That question is the whole business. Everything else is arithmetic.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
<!-- SHIFT -->
<Section bg="navy">
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <Label> The shift </Label>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-4xl">
      Move the steady beasts off the meter.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-white/80">
      Hybrid by design. Keep public cloud where burst and managed services earn
      their keep. Move steady, data-heavy, and GPU-bound workloads when the unit
      economics say so — not when the ideology does.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-8">
      <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">What you keep</div>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-white/80">
        <li>Kubernetes, GitOps, IaC</li>
        <li>Previews, secrets, environments</li>
        <li>Ship rituals engineers already expect</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-electric p-8 text-white">
      <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">What you gain</div>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2">
        <li>Predictable marginal cost</li>
        <li>No egress ransom</li>
        <li>GPU capacity you control</li>
        <li>Data residency and audit</li>
        <li>Cost reports finance can read</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
<!-- LADDER -->
<Section bg="warm">
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <Label color="signal">The ladder</Label>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-4xl">
      Assess → Pilot → Build → Operate.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-slate">
      Each stage is a fixed scope with exit criteria. No big-bang migration. No
      religious wars. The next stage starts only if the last one earned it.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {ladder.map(({ data: s }) => (
      <div class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-rule bg-white p-6">
        <div class="text-xs font-bold text-electric">{s.step}</div>
        <div class="mt-2 text-xl font-black">{s.name}</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate">{s.duration}</div>
        <div class="mt-2 text-sm font-semibold text-navy">{s.price}</div>
        <p class="mt-4 flex-1 text-sm text-slate">{s.summary}</p>
        <div class="mt-5 text-xs font-semibold text-navy">Exit: {s.exit}</div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <Button href="/engagements">See full engagements</Button>
  </div>
</Section>
<!-- PROOF -->
<Section bg="navy">
  <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <Label>Proof</Label>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-4xl">
        We run what we sell.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg font-medium">
        You won't be Reardon Systems' first private platform customer. We already are.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-white/75">
        Reardon Systems operates its own stack — self-hosted platforms,
        Tailscale-first access, and selective repatriation for workloads that
        should never have been metered by the hour. The tools we build for
        ourselves are the same patterns we sell: private by default, GitOps from
        day one, and software that keeps working when the environment doesn't
        cooperate.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-8">
        <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-electric">Shipped</div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg font-medium">
          SpecOps is our inspection product: a diagnostic scanner for the home.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-white/75">
          Onsite defect capture, reports that generate on the same visit, and an
          app that works in the crawlspace when the signal drops. Live in private
          beta with home inspection teams.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-white/60">
          SpecOps runs on the same private platform patterns we build for
          clients. It's not a side project. It's the proof that the stack works
          under real load, with real users, in an environment where downtime has
          consequences.
        </p>
        <a href="/products/specops"
           class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-electric hover:text-white">
          See SpecOps →
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8 text-white/60">
        Not anti-cloud. Anti-default.
        <span class="font-semibold text-white">Private where it pays. Public where it bursts.</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
<!-- FAQ -->
<Section>
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <Label>FAQ</Label>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-4xl">
      Questions we get asked.
    </h2>
  </div>
  {faqs && (
    <div class="mt-10 divide-y divide-rule border-y border-rule">
      {faqs.data.items.map((f) => (
        <details class="group py-5">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between">
            <span class="font-semibold">{f.q}</span>
            <span class="ml-4 text-electric transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">＋</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-slate">{f.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  )}
</Section>
<!-- FINAL CTA -->
<Section bg="warm">
  <div class="grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-5xl">
        Show us the bill that hurts.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-xl text-lg text-slate">
        Mid-market teams with real hyperscaler spend. Not startups guessing. Not
        enterprises buying another transformation program.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate/80">
        We reply in plain language. Infra pass-through stays separate. Optional
        savings-share when incentives should align.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <Button href="/contact">Start with an Assessment</Button>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
</Base>
